-- Euclid's lemma for a natural prime dividing an integer product, the two
-- square roots of one modulo a prime, primes are not squares, and a natural
-- d with x² = d y² (y > 0) is a square.
-- Part of the Arithmetic blueprint.
-- Planned home: NumberTheory/IntegerPrime.
